# March Update!

SquirrelJME now has a single standalone Jar which is multi-platform, so now
it will be easier to run it without having to fully know what your system is.

I decided to just merge in the calendar implementation despite it being
incomplete, since it was a very long-lived branch that I just wanted to close.
A large number of DoJa software requires a calendar implementation, so this
should be an initial first-step for that.

Other than that, there has been continued work on NanoCoat which is
progressing well. Currently, I am working on the main startup sequence for
applications.
